{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== LIVE EVIDENCE COMPLETE. BOTH OF THIS STORY'S REMAINING CELLS ARE GREEN. ===\n\nHARNESS RUN 30772461871, job \"jira DC harness smoke (real Jira Data Center, ephemeral)\", job id\n91561874505, against main @ bd3de0f864 — the first tree carrying EVERYTHING this story depended on:\nd067's status-transition fix, the 8d68 inbound-mint fix, and this story's own oracle rewrite.\nDuration 1674.11s. Result: **1 failed, 48 passed**, with the all-skip canary confirming nothing was\nsilently skipped:\n    [jira-live-canary] collected=49 executed=49 skipped=0\n\nTHE TWO CELLS THIS STORY OWED, BOTH EXPLICITLY PASSED:\n    PASSED tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py::test_outbound_mutation_round_trips[04-transition-status]\n    PASSED tests/external/live_jira_dc/test_dc_mutations.py::test_the_inbound_assignee_mints_a_jira_family_identity\n\nTHE ASSIGNEE CELL'S GREEN IS THE MEANINGFUL ONE, and it is green WITHOUT ANY ASSERTION WEAKENED —\nits oracle is byte-unchanged since changes 1226/1227. It failed on run 30767546938 (pre-fix, main @\nd72c4777d3) with \"THE PASS MINTED NOTHING\", which is what led to filing and fixing\n8d68-a740-4f56-4b3a. Same harness, same instance shape, same oracle; the only difference is the\nproduct fix. That is a controlled before/after, not a bare green.\nThe transition cell is now green for the THIRD consecutive run (30765232591, 30767546938, 30772461871).\n\nTHE SINGLE FAILURE IS UNRELATED TO THIS STORY AND IS NOT A REGRESSION:\n    FAILED test_transport.py::test_a_rekeyed_issue_resolves_by_id_and_records_what_the_stale_key_returns\nIt failed on its OWN SETUP ASSERTION with \"assert 'RBJDRDZ' != 'RBJDRDZ'\". Cause, read from source:\ntest_transport.py:515 derives the rename target as (key[:-1] + \"Z\"), and harness project keys are\nRBJ + 4 random letters (conftest.py:154,185). This run drew a key ENDING IN Z, so the derived \"new\"\nkey was byte-identical to the original and the cell correctly refused to proceed. It is flaky by\nconstruction at roughly 1 run in 26, and it passed the two previous runs only because their draws did\nnot end in Z. Nothing merged in that tree touches test_transport.py, project-key generation or the\nrename path. Filed as [rebar:d582-fd5a-7ece-4c32] (discovered_from this story). Worth noting the cell\nFAILED SAFE — its setup assertion is what made a would-be no-op rename legible instead of silently\nproving nothing.\n\nEVERY FAILURE THIS STORY ORIGINALLY SURFACED IS NOW RESOLVED: 727f and d103 (closed), b9b8, d067\n(closed), the inbound-link cell (proven NOT a product defect — the failing run predated b9b8's\npriming pass, and the skip it exposed is structural and correct by phase order), and the assignee\ncell (this story's own vacuous oracle, rewritten, which then exposed the real 8d68 defect)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785716420686907001,"uuid":"89fb452b-4a56-4c94-acf7-83c45dbf587c"}